<meta name='description' content='The nearest 50000 stars with a known distance, every star of magnitude 6.5 or brighter and every named star, at true 3D positions. 1 unit = 1 light-year (SkyScale stays at 1: X_ITE 16.7.1 crashed the page when the splats were scaled by 300 or more). Axes: equatorial J2000 stored as X3D (X, Y, Z) = (y, z, x). Splat sigma = angular sigma times distance, angular sigma = 0.10 deg x 10^(-0.13 (m - 2)) clipped to 0.012..0.42 deg; opacity 0.95 x 10^(-0.20 (m - 4.2)) clipped to 0.08..0.95. 179 halo splats follow the 8714 bright stars. Colour from B-V. Positions are J2000: no proper motion in this file. SunGlow and MoonGlow are stage lights for the baked plateau (azimuth 248 and 300 degrees), not ephemeris positions.'/>
